{"title":"BBCode:Tutorial","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><center>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"border:1px solid black; background:#CEE0F2;text-align:center;\" align=\"center\">\n\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#B0C4DE;\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=BBCode\" title=\"BBCode\">BBCode</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=BBCode\" title=\"BBCode\">BBCode</a> - <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">Tutorial</a> - <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=List_of_BBCodes\" title=\"List of BBCodes\">List of BBCodes</a> - <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Aops_font\" title=\"Aops font\">AoPS Font</a>\n</td></tr></tbody></table></center>\n<div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#The_Basics\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">The Basics</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Writing_Messages_in_the_AoPS_Community\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Writing Messages in the AoPS Community</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#The_Buttons\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">The Buttons</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-3 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#The_Bold_Button\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.1.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">The Bold Button</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-3 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#The_Italics_Button\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.1.2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">The Italics Button</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-3 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#The_Underline_Button\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.1.3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">The Underline Button</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-3 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#The_Quote_Button\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.1.4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">The Quote Button</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-3 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#The_Size_Button\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.1.5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">The Size Button</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-3 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#The_Hide_Button\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.1.6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">The Hide Button</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-3 tocsection-10\"><a href=\"#The_Code_Button\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.1.7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">The Code Button</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-3 tocsection-11\"><a href=\"#The_Image_Button\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.1.8</span> <span class=\"toctext\">The Image Button</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-3 tocsection-12\"><a href=\"#The_URL_Button\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.1.9</span> <span class=\"toctext\">The URL Button</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-13\"><a href=\"#Other_Tags\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Other Tags</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-3 tocsection-14\"><a href=\"#Unordered_List\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.2.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Unordered List</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-3 tocsection-15\"><a href=\"#Ordered_List\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.2.2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Ordered List</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-3 tocsection-16\"><a href=\"#Python_Tags\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.2.3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Python Tags</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-3 tocsection-17\"><a href=\"#AoPS_Font\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.2.4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">AoPS Font</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-3 tocsection-18\"><a href=\"#Lines\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.2.5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Lines</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-3 tocsection-19\"><a href=\"#Strike_Through\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.2.6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Strike Through</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-3 tocsection-20\"><a href=\"#Math\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.2.7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Math</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-3 tocsection-21\"><a href=\"#Tip_Tag\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.2.8</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Tip Tag</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h1><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"The_Basics\">The Basics</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=BBCode:Tutorial&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: The Basics\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h1>\n<p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Bbcode\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Bbcode\">BBCode</a> is a way to format text in forum posts. It is in some ways similar to HTML. It uses tags, which are little pieces of code enclosed in brackets, such as [b] to make bold text. For every tag, you need a closing tag too. The closing tag is the same as the opening tag except that it has a / symbol at the front. For example, the tag [/b] is code for \"stop making the text bold.\" There is text between the opening and closing tags, that is the text that is modified by the tags. \n</p><p>For example, If you want to say \"I love pizza\" and want the word \"love\" to be in bold, you would type\n</p>\n<dl><dd><code>I [b]love[/b] pizza</code>.</dd></dl>\n<p>This would create, \"I <b>love</b> pizza.\"\n</p><p>Below are some of the most commonly used BBCode tags around AoPS forums. For a comprehensive list of all BBCode tags, see <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=List_of_BBCodes\" title=\"List of BBCodes\">List of BBCode tags</a>.\n</p>\n<h1><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Writing_Messages_in_the_AoPS_Community\">Writing Messages in the AoPS Community</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=BBCode:Tutorial&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Writing Messages in the AoPS Community\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h1>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"The_Buttons\">The Buttons</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=BBCode:Tutorial&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: The Buttons\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><span typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:Post_a_reply.PNG\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/1/10/Post_a_reply.PNG/800px-Post_a_reply.PNG\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"800\" height=\"174\" class=\"mw-file-element\" srcset=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/1/10/Post_a_reply.PNG/1200px-Post_a_reply.PNG 1.5x, https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/1/10/Post_a_reply.PNG 2x\" /></a></span>\n</p><p>This is a picture of what you see when you create a topic or post a reply. On very small screens (such as a smartphone) these buttons will not appear, so you will have to type the BBCode in manually.\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"The_Bold_Button\">The Bold Button</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=BBCode:Tutorial&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: The Bold Button\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>The <span typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:Bold_button.jpeg\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/2/20/Bold_button.jpeg/25px-Bold_button.jpeg\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"25\" height=\"27\" class=\"mw-file-element\" srcset=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/2/20/Bold_button.jpeg/38px-Bold_button.jpeg 1.5x, https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/2/20/Bold_button.jpeg/50px-Bold_button.jpeg 2x\" /></a></span> button is the bold button. When you click on it, your screen should look like this:\n</p><p><span typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:Clicked_on_bold_button.PNG\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/3/3d/Clicked_on_bold_button.PNG/800px-Clicked_on_bold_button.PNG\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"800\" height=\"171\" class=\"mw-file-element\" srcset=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/3/3d/Clicked_on_bold_button.PNG/1200px-Clicked_on_bold_button.PNG 1.5x, https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/3/3d/Clicked_on_bold_button.PNG 2x\" /></a></span>\n</p><p>These are called bold tags. Then, you can type in any text you want:\n<span typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:Type_in_bold_text.PNG\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/2/2a/Type_in_bold_text.PNG/800px-Type_in_bold_text.PNG\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"800\" height=\"149\" class=\"mw-file-element\" srcset=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/2/2a/Type_in_bold_text.PNG/1200px-Type_in_bold_text.PNG 1.5x, https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/2/2a/Type_in_bold_text.PNG 2x\" /></a></span>\n</p><p>When you submit it, it should look like this:\n<span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:Submitted_Bold_Text.PNG\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/e/e3/Submitted_Bold_Text.PNG\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"133\" height=\"38\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"The_Italics_Button\">The Italics Button</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=BBCode:Tutorial&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: The Italics Button\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>The <span typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:Italics_button.jpeg\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/7/77/Italics_button.jpeg/25px-Italics_button.jpeg\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"25\" height=\"25\" class=\"mw-file-element\" srcset=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/7/77/Italics_button.jpeg/38px-Italics_button.jpeg 1.5x, https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/7/77/Italics_button.jpeg/50px-Italics_button.jpeg 2x\" /></a></span> button is the italics button. When you click on it, your screen should look like this:\n</p><p><span typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:Clicked_on_italics_button.jpeg\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/1/1e/Clicked_on_italics_button.jpeg/700px-Clicked_on_italics_button.jpeg\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"700\" height=\"166\" class=\"mw-file-element\" srcset=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/1/1e/Clicked_on_italics_button.jpeg/1050px-Clicked_on_italics_button.jpeg 1.5x, https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/1/1e/Clicked_on_italics_button.jpeg/1400px-Clicked_on_italics_button.jpeg 2x\" /></a></span>\n</p><p>Then you can type in your italicized message:\n</p><p><span typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:Italics_message.jpeg\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/9/9c/Italics_message.jpeg/200px-Italics_message.jpeg\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"200\" height=\"94\" class=\"mw-file-element\" srcset=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/9/9c/Italics_message.jpeg/300px-Italics_message.jpeg 1.5x, https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/9/9c/Italics_message.jpeg/400px-Italics_message.jpeg 2x\" /></a></span>\n</p><p>When you submit, it should look like this:\n</p><p><span typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:Italics_result.jpeg\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/1/1e/Italics_result.jpeg/700px-Italics_result.jpeg\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"700\" height=\"127\" class=\"mw-file-element\" srcset=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/1/1e/Italics_result.jpeg/1050px-Italics_result.jpeg 1.5x, https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/1/1e/Italics_result.jpeg/1400px-Italics_result.jpeg 2x\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"The_Underline_Button\">The Underline Button</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=BBCode:Tutorial&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: The Underline Button\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>The <span typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:Underline_button.jpeg\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/9/9e/Underline_button.jpeg/25px-Underline_button.jpeg\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"25\" height=\"22\" class=\"mw-file-element\" srcset=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/9/9e/Underline_button.jpeg/38px-Underline_button.jpeg 1.5x, https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/9/9e/Underline_button.jpeg/50px-Underline_button.jpeg 2x\" /></a></span> button is for underlining text. When you click on it, the symbols [u] and [/u] appear. Then you can type in whatever you want to be underlined:\n</p><p><span typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:Underline_typing.jpeg\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/e/e5/Underline_typing.jpeg/300px-Underline_typing.jpeg\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"300\" height=\"169\" class=\"mw-file-element\" srcset=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/e/e5/Underline_typing.jpeg/450px-Underline_typing.jpeg 1.5x, https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/e/e5/Underline_typing.jpeg/600px-Underline_typing.jpeg 2x\" /></a></span>\n</p><p>When you submit it, it should look like this:\n</p><p><span typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:Underline_result.jpeg\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/9/92/Underline_result.jpeg/700px-Underline_result.jpeg\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"700\" height=\"126\" class=\"mw-file-element\" srcset=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/9/92/Underline_result.jpeg 1.5x\" /></a></span>\n</p><p>Note: you can also highlight text and then click the underline button.\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"The_Quote_Button\">The Quote Button</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=BBCode:Tutorial&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: The Quote Button\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>The <span typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:Quote_button.jpeg\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/2/25/Quote_button.jpeg/25px-Quote_button.jpeg\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"25\" height=\"23\" class=\"mw-file-element\" srcset=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/2/25/Quote_button.jpeg/38px-Quote_button.jpeg 1.5x, https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/2/25/Quote_button.jpeg/50px-Quote_button.jpeg 2x\" /></a></span> button is for quoting text. You can write an anonymous quote, or quote a specific user or person. When you click on it, you get [quote] and [/quote]. Then type in the quote:\n</p><p><span typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:Typing_generic_quote.jpeg\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/8/80/Typing_generic_quote.jpeg/300px-Typing_generic_quote.jpeg\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"300\" height=\"169\" class=\"mw-file-element\" srcset=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/8/80/Typing_generic_quote.jpeg/450px-Typing_generic_quote.jpeg 1.5x, https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/8/80/Typing_generic_quote.jpeg/600px-Typing_generic_quote.jpeg 2x\" /></a></span>\n</p><p>When you hit submit, it looks like this:\n</p><p><span typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:Published_generic_quote.jpeg\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/a/a2/Published_generic_quote.jpeg/600px-Published_generic_quote.jpeg\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"600\" height=\"116\" class=\"mw-file-element\" srcset=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/a/a2/Published_generic_quote.jpeg/900px-Published_generic_quote.jpeg 1.5x, https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/a/a2/Published_generic_quote.jpeg/1200px-Published_generic_quote.jpeg 2x\" /></a></span>\n</p><p>Or, alternatively, you can say who quoted it:\n</p><p><span typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:Specific_quote_typing.jpeg\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/d/dc/Specific_quote_typing.jpeg/400px-Specific_quote_typing.jpeg\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"400\" height=\"225\" class=\"mw-file-element\" srcset=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/d/dc/Specific_quote_typing.jpeg/600px-Specific_quote_typing.jpeg 1.5x, https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/d/dc/Specific_quote_typing.jpeg/800px-Specific_quote_typing.jpeg 2x\" /></a></span>\n</p><p>And you get this:\n</p><p><span typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:Specific_quote_published.jpeg\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/2/29/Specific_quote_published.jpeg/600px-Specific_quote_published.jpeg\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"600\" height=\"137\" class=\"mw-file-element\" srcset=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/2/29/Specific_quote_published.jpeg/900px-Specific_quote_published.jpeg 1.5x, https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/2/29/Specific_quote_published.jpeg 2x\" /></a></span>\n</p><p>You can also quote a post by clicking this button in the forum.\n</p><p><span typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:Arrow_to_quote_button.jpeg\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/0/0d/Arrow_to_quote_button.jpeg/650px-Arrow_to_quote_button.jpeg\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"650\" height=\"149\" class=\"mw-file-element\" srcset=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/0/0d/Arrow_to_quote_button.jpeg/975px-Arrow_to_quote_button.jpeg 1.5x, https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/0/0d/Arrow_to_quote_button.jpeg/1300px-Arrow_to_quote_button.jpeg 2x\" /></a></span>\n</p><p>You will be taken to a reply page that looks like this:\n</p><p><span typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:Specific_quote_typing.jpeg\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/d/dc/Specific_quote_typing.jpeg/400px-Specific_quote_typing.jpeg\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"400\" height=\"225\" class=\"mw-file-element\" srcset=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/d/dc/Specific_quote_typing.jpeg/600px-Specific_quote_typing.jpeg 1.5x, https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/d/dc/Specific_quote_typing.jpeg/800px-Specific_quote_typing.jpeg 2x\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"The_Size_Button\">The Size Button</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=BBCode:Tutorial&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: The Size Button\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>The button with the three T's is for controlling the font size. You can click on either \"Too Small\", \"Small\", \"Medium\", \"Large\", or \"Too Large\" depending on what size you want. After you click on one of them, you should get something like [size=75] and [/size].\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"The_Hide_Button\">The Hide Button</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=BBCode:Tutorial&amp;action=edit&amp;section=9\" title=\"Edit section: The Hide Button\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>The <span typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:Hide_button.jpeg\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/9/91/Hide_button.jpeg/25px-Hide_button.jpeg\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"25\" height=\"19\" class=\"mw-file-element\" srcset=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/9/91/Hide_button.jpeg/38px-Hide_button.jpeg 1.5x, https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/9/91/Hide_button.jpeg/50px-Hide_button.jpeg 2x\" /></a></span> button embeds text in a little interactive clicky. This is useful if you want your text only visible if the reader wants to see it. For example, if you are answering a math problem, you can hide the text so that you don't give away the answer to someone who doesn't want to know it.\n</p><p>Start by clicking the hide button. You should get [hide] and [/hide].\nThen put in your text:\n</p><p><span typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:Type_hide_generic.jpeg\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/0/05/Type_hide_generic.jpeg/600px-Type_hide_generic.jpeg\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"600\" height=\"175\" class=\"mw-file-element\" srcset=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/0/05/Type_hide_generic.jpeg/900px-Type_hide_generic.jpeg 1.5x, https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/0/05/Type_hide_generic.jpeg/1200px-Type_hide_generic.jpeg 2x\" /></a></span>\n</p><p>When you submit, you get this:\n</p><p><span typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:Click_for_hidden_text.jpeg\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/7/79/Click_for_hidden_text.jpeg/400px-Click_for_hidden_text.jpeg\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"400\" height=\"81\" class=\"mw-file-element\" srcset=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/7/79/Click_for_hidden_text.jpeg/600px-Click_for_hidden_text.jpeg 1.5x, https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/7/79/Click_for_hidden_text.jpeg/800px-Click_for_hidden_text.jpeg 2x\" /></a></span>\n</p><p>If you click on the words \"Hidden Text\", you get this:\n</p><p><span typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:Open_hidden_text.jpeg\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/6/6d/Open_hidden_text.jpeg/400px-Open_hidden_text.jpeg\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"400\" height=\"85\" class=\"mw-file-element\" srcset=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/6/6d/Open_hidden_text.jpeg/600px-Open_hidden_text.jpeg 1.5x, https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/6/6d/Open_hidden_text.jpeg/800px-Open_hidden_text.jpeg 2x\" /></a></span><br />\n</p><p>Or you can label your hidden text. First, write in the code of the hidden text something like:\n</p>\n<dl><dd><code>[hide=answer]Because 6x=y, and y is 6, then x must be 1.[/hide]</code></dd></dl>\n<p><br />\nAnd then submit, you get:<br />\n</p><p><span typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:Labeled_closed_hidden_text.jpeg\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/5/51/Labeled_closed_hidden_text.jpeg/300px-Labeled_closed_hidden_text.jpeg\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"300\" height=\"82\" class=\"mw-file-element\" srcset=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/5/51/Labeled_closed_hidden_text.jpeg/450px-Labeled_closed_hidden_text.jpeg 1.5x, https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/5/51/Labeled_closed_hidden_text.jpeg 2x\" /></a></span>\n</p><p><span typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:Published_open_hidden_text.jpeg\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/d/d6/Published_open_hidden_text.jpeg/400px-Published_open_hidden_text.jpeg\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"400\" height=\"63\" class=\"mw-file-element\" srcset=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/d/d6/Published_open_hidden_text.jpeg/600px-Published_open_hidden_text.jpeg 1.5x, https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/d/d6/Published_open_hidden_text.jpeg/800px-Published_open_hidden_text.jpeg 2x\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"The_Code_Button\">The Code Button</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=BBCode:Tutorial&amp;action=edit&amp;section=10\" title=\"Edit section: The Code Button\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>The <span typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:Code_button.JPEG\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/6/6e/Code_button.JPEG/25px-Code_button.JPEG\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"25\" height=\"20\" class=\"mw-file-element\" srcset=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/6/6e/Code_button.JPEG 1.5x\" /></a></span> button is for posting code that you don't want to be rendered, ie <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=LaTeX\" title=\"LaTeX\">LaTeX</a> or <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=BBCode\" title=\"BBCode\">BBCode</a>. When you click on it, your screen should display:\n</p>\n<dl><dd><code>[code][/code]</code></dd></dl>\n<p>Type in your code:\n</p>\n<dl><dd><code>[code]$10+9=21$[/code]</code></dd></dl>\n<p>And it should display:\n</p><p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:Code_submitted.JPEG\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/Code_submitted.JPEG\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"309\" height=\"94\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p><p>Notice that the LaTeX code is not rendered; that is, it does not show up as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/e/2/be2eb2c9e54b6873abe643eff1b08df281b680be.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10+9=21$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"90\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>If you want a specific color of code do [ code language ][/ code language ] such as [js][/js].\n</p><p>Another way for posting stuff that you don't want to be rendered, is the [verbatim][/verbatim] tags (not implemented on the top BBCode bar in the forums). There will be no grey box that there is when using [code][/code], and it will not automatically be placed on its own line.\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"The_Image_Button\">The Image Button</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=BBCode:Tutorial&amp;action=edit&amp;section=11\" title=\"Edit section: The Image Button\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>The <span typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:Image_Button.JPEG\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/4/42/Image_Button.JPEG\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"25\" height=\"21\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span> button is for embedding images in posts. If you have this image:<br />\n<a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"http://artofproblemsolving.com/assets/images/logo-ludicrous.gif\">http://artofproblemsolving.com/assets/images/logo-ludicrous.gif</a><br />\nAnd you want it to show up like this:\n</p><p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AoPS_loading.GIF\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/f/fb/AoPS_loading.GIF\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"40\" height=\"40\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p><p>You use [img] tags. Click on the <span typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:Image_Button.JPEG\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/4/42/Image_Button.JPEG\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"25\" height=\"21\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span> button and your screen should show:\n</p>\n<dl><dd><code>[img][/img]</code></dd></dl>\n<p>Now insert the link to the image. Make sure it is a <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Wiki/index.php/Direct_Image_Link\">direct link</a>.<br />\n</p>\n<dl><dd><code>[img]http://artofproblemsolving.com/assets/images/logo-ludicrous.gif[/img]</code><br /></dd></dl>\n<p>When you submit, you should get the image!<br />\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"The_URL_Button\">The URL Button</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=BBCode:Tutorial&amp;action=edit&amp;section=12\" title=\"Edit section: The URL Button\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>The <span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:Link_Button.PNG\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/1/15/Link_Button.PNG\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"27\" height=\"25\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span> button is for parsing and naming URLs. If you click it, your screen should look like this:\n</p>\n<dl><dd><code>[url][/url]</code></dd></dl>\n<p>Now type in your URL:<br />\n</p>\n<dl><dd><code>[url]http://www.aops.com/[/url]</code></dd></dl>\n<p>When you submit it, it should be parsed, like this:\n</p><p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.aops.com/\">http://www.aops.com/</a>\n</p><p>Alternatively, if you want a link that goes somewhere but is not actually named the URL, do this:\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<dl><dd><code>[url=http://www.aops.com/] Click here.[/url]</code></dd></dl>\n<p>You get\n</p><p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.aops.com/\">Click here.</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Other_Tags\">Other Tags</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=BBCode:Tutorial&amp;action=edit&amp;section=13\" title=\"Edit section: Other Tags\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>There are other things you can do with BBCode that do not have buttons in the AoPS community.\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Unordered_List\">Unordered List</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=BBCode:Tutorial&amp;action=edit&amp;section=14\" title=\"Edit section: Unordered List\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>An unordered list is a simple bullet point list. To use it, you simply use the [list] tag. Before each new list item, type [*]. The [*] tag is for a list item. You don't need a closing tag for the [*] tag. For example, typing\n</p>\n<dl><dd><code></code></dd><code>\n<dd>[list]</dd>\n<dd>[*] pizza</dd>\n<dd>[*] pasta</dd>\n<dd>[*] rice</dd>\n<dd>[*] cereal</dd>\n</code><dd><code>[/list]</code></dd></dl>\n<p>creates:\n</p>\n<ul>\n<li>pizza</li>\n<li>pasta</li>\n<li>rice</li>\n<li>cereal</li></ul>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Ordered_List\">Ordered List</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=BBCode:Tutorial&amp;action=edit&amp;section=15\" title=\"Edit section: Ordered List\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>The BBcode for the following uses the [list] tag. To tell you want a numbered list, type [list=1]. For example, typing, \n</p>\n<dl><dd><code></code></dd><code>\n<dd>Top 10 most important people of all time:</dd>\n<dd>[list=1]</dd>\n<dd>[*]GMAAS</dd>\n<dd>[*]Gauss</dd>\n<dd>[*]Hilbert</dd>\n<dd>[*]Leibniz</dd>\n<dd>[*]Cantor</dd>\n<dd>[*]Rusczyk</dd>\n<dd>[*]Patrick</dd>\n<dd>[*]Newton</dd>\n<dd>[*]Washington</dd>\n<dd>[*]Edison</dd>\n</code><dd><code>[/list]</code></dd></dl>\n<p>creates\n</p>\n<dl><dd>Top 10 most important people of all time:</dd></dl>\n<ol>\n<dl><dd><li>GMAAS</li></dd>\n<dd><li>GMAAS</li></dd>\n<dd><li>GMAAS</li></dd>\n<dd><li>GMAAS</li></dd>\n<dd><li>GMAAS</li></dd>\n<dd><li>v</li></dd>\n<dd><li>GMAAS</li></dd>\n<dd><li>GMAAS</li></dd>\n<dd><li>GMAAS</li></dd>\n<dd><li>GMAAS</li></dd></dl>\n</ol>\n<p>Alternatively, if you want to make a lettered list, start with [list=A] or [list=a]. For a roman numeral list, use [list=i] or [list=I].\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Python_Tags\">Python Tags</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=BBCode:Tutorial&amp;action=edit&amp;section=16\" title=\"Edit section: Python Tags\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>If you are taking an AoPS programming with a Python class, you may need to post some Python code in the class forum. To do this you use the [python] tags.\nThese tags are like the [code] tags except that they show the python code in colors.\nFor example, typing\n</p>\n<dl><dd><code>[python]</code></dd><code>\n<dd>print(\"hello\"+\" world\")</dd>\n<dd>print(\"Hello, world!\")</dd>\n<dd>[/python]</dd></code></dl><code></code><p><code></code>\n</p><p>Yields\n</p><p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:Python_tags.PNG\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/f/f0/Python_tags.PNG\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"356\" height=\"96\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p><p>If you want to have a Python renderer in a post in a forum, you can use [pywindow] tags. \nFor example, typing\n</p>\n<dl><dd><code>[pywindow]</code></dd><code>\n<dd>print(\"Hello World!\")</dd>\n</code><dd><code>[/pywindow]</code></dd></dl>\n<p>yields a code box that can be run and edited.\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"AoPS_Font\">AoPS Font</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=BBCode:Tutorial&amp;action=edit&amp;section=17\" title=\"Edit section: AoPS Font\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p><i>Main article: <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=AoPS_font\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"AoPS font\">AoPS font</a></i>\n</p><p>Say you want to type the <span class=\"aops-font\">Y</span> symbol on a forum post. You can use the [aops][/aops] tags to create symbols like this. For example, typing \n</p>\n<dl><dd><code>[aops]Y[/aops]</code></dd></dl>\n<p>makes the  <span class=\"aops-font\">Y</span> symbol. For a guide to how to type other symbols, see the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=AoPS_font\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"AoPS font\">AoPS font</a> page.\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Lines\">Lines</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=BBCode:Tutorial&amp;action=edit&amp;section=18\" title=\"Edit section: Lines\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>If you wish to have a line that spans the entire width of the page, you can use the [rule] tag. For example, try typing\n</p>\n<dl><dd><code>[rule]</code></dd></dl>\n<p>in <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/community/c67_test_forum\">The Test Forum</a>. Should you not wish to use <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=BBCode\" title=\"BBCode\">BBCode</a>, you can use 5 or more dashes instead.\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Strike_Through\">Strike Through</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=BBCode:Tutorial&amp;action=edit&amp;section=19\" title=\"Edit section: Strike Through\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>The Strike Through tag looks like this:\n</p>\n<ol>\nTags:\n<li><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:Strike_Through.jpg\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/7/70/Strike_Through.jpg\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"110\" height=\"71\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span></li>\nContent:\n<li><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:Strike_Through2.jpg\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d4/Strike_Through2.jpg\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"155\" height=\"101\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span></li>\nResult:\n<li><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:Strike_Through3.jpg\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/4/4d/Strike_Through3.jpg\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"130\" height=\"81\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span></li>\n</ol>\n<p>This is how to strikethrough.\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Math\">Math</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=BBCode:Tutorial&amp;action=edit&amp;section=20\" title=\"Edit section: Math\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>The Math tag looks like this:\n</p>\n<ol>\nTags:\n<li><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:Math_BBCode_tag.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/8/81/Math_BBCode_tag.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"95\" height=\"22\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span></li>\nContent:\n<li><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:Math_BBCode_tag_2.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/4/42/Math_BBCode_tag_2.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"144\" height=\"19\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span></li>\nResult:\n<li><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:Math_BBCode_tag_3.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/7/7e/Math_BBCode_tag_3.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"42\" height=\"45\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span></li>\n</ol>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Tip_Tag\">Tip Tag</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=BBCode:Tutorial&amp;action=edit&amp;section=21\" title=\"Edit section: Tip Tag\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>The tip tag is basically a hide tag, except it displays the embedded text when you hover over it.\nTo use it, use [tip]This is the text![/tip], and replace the text inside the tip with whatever you want.\nWhen you submit you get this: \n<span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:Tip-tag.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/e/ee/Tip-tag.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"111\" height=\"36\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p><p>When you hover:\n<span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:Tip-tag-hover.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/5/58/Tip-tag-hover.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"118\" height=\"64\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p><p>You can name tip tags with this code:\n[tip=Tip Title]content[/tip]\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018040358\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.116 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.185 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 142/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 295/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 2/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 321/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    8.411      1 Template:BBCode\n100.00%    8.411      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:10327:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261018040358 and revision id 282415. Rendering was triggered because: page-view\n -->\n</div>"}